###  Static site generation
You can generate a static version of your search page at build time using Next’s [`getStaticProps`](https://nextjs.org/docs/basic-features/data-fetching/get-static-props). Static site generation (or pre-rendering) is essentially the same thing as [server-side rendering](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/going-further/server-side-rendering/react#server-side-rendering), except the latter happens at request time, while the former happens at build time. You can use the same [`InstantSearchSSRProvider`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/ssr-provider/react) and [`getServerState`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/server-state/react) APIs for both [server-side rendering](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/going-further/server-side-rendering/react#server-side-rendering) and static site generation.
