sortBy
string[] | (a: FacetValue, b: FacetValue) => number
How to sort refinements. Must be one or more of the following strings:
  * `"count"` (same as `"count:desc"`)
  * `"count:asc"`
  * `"count:desc"`
  * `"name"` (same as `"name:asc"`)
  * `"name:asc"`
  * `"name:desc"`
  * `"isRefined"` (same as `"isRefined:asc"`)
  * `"isRefined:asc"`
  * `"isRefined:desc"`

You can also use a sort function that behaves like the standard JavaScript [`compareFunction`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/sort#Syntax).When you don’t set this parameter, and you’ve set `facetOrdering` for this facet in `renderingContent`, facets are sorted using `facetOrdering` and use the default order as a fallback.
In some situations, refined facet values might not be present in the data returned by Algolia.
