**Starting from v4.9.0, Vue InstantSearch can load[`search-insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights) for you so the [`insightsClient`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/insights/vue#param-insights-client) option is no longer required.** If you prefer loading it yourself, make sure to update [`search-insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights) to at least v2.4.0 and forward the reference to [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/vue#param-insights). If you’re using the UMD bundle with a `<script>` tag, make sure to update the full code snippet (not just the version):
