By default, the analyzed period includes the last eight days including the current day. **Required ACL:** `analytics`
#### Authorizations
x-algolia-application-id
string
header
required
Your Algolia application ID.
x-algolia-api-key
string
header
required
Your Algolia API key with the necessary permissions to make the request. Permissions are controlled through access control lists (ACL) and access restrictions. The required ACL to make a request is listed in each endpoint's reference.
#### Query Parameters
index
string
required
Index name.
Example:
`"ALGOLIA_INDEX_NAME"`
endDate
string
End date of the period to analyze, in `YYYY-MM-DD` format.
Example:
`"2023-01-21"`
startDate
string
Start date of the period to analyze, in `YYYY-MM-DD` format.
Example:
`"2022-09-19"`
tags
string
Tags by which to segment the analytics.
You can combine multiple tags with `OR` and `AND`. Tags must be URL-encoded. For more information, see [Segment your analytics data](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/search-analytics/guides/segments).
#### Response
200
application/json
OK
count
integer
default:0
required
Number of tracked searches. Tracked searches are search requests where the `clickAnalytics` parameter is true.
Example:
dates
dailyNoClickRates · object[]
required
Daily no click rates.
Show child attributes
noClickCount
integer
required
Number of times this search was returned as a result without any click.
Required range: `x >= 1`
Example:
`15`
rate
number<double>
required
No click rate: calculated as the number of tracked searches without clicks divided by the number of tracked searches.
Required range: `0 <= x <= 1`
Example:
`0.15`
