  // Optional parameters
  limit?: number,
  showMore?: boolean,
  showMoreLimit?: number,
  sortBy?: string[] | function,
  templates?: object,
  cssClasses?: object,
  transformItems?: function,
});

```

##  Import
Package manager
CDN

```
import { menu } from "instantsearch.js/es/widgets";

```


```
const { menu } = instantsearch.widgets;
// or directly use instantsearch.widgets.menu()

```

## See this widget in action
Preview this widget and its behavior.
##  About this widget
The `menu` widget displays a menu that lets users choose a single value for a specific attribute.
The `menu` widget uses a hierarchical refinement internally, so it can’t refine values that include the default separator (`>`). To support these values, use the [`hierarchicalMenu`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/hierarchical-menu/js) widget instead.
###  Requirements
The [`attribute`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/menu/js#param-attribute) provided to the widget must be in attributes for faceting, either on the [dashboard](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/managing-results/refine-results/faceting/how-to/declaring-attributes-for-faceting-with-dashboard) or using the [`attributesForFaceting`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/attributesForFaceting) parameter with the API.
##  Examples
JavaScript

```
menu({
  container: "#menu",
  attribute: "categories",
});

```

##  Options
container
string | HTMLElement
required
The CSS Selector of the DOM element inside which the widget is inserted.
string
HTMLElement

