##  Enable the `insights` option
To automatically send events, turn the [`insights` option](https://www.algolia.com/doc/ui-libraries/autocomplete/api-reference/autocomplete-js/autocomplete#param-insights) to `true` in your autocomplete instance.
JavaScript

```
// ...

autocomplete({
  container: "#autocomplete",
  placeholder: "Search products",
  openOnFocus: true,
  insights: true,
  getSources({ query }) {
    // ...
  },
});

// ...

```

To identify users consistently, such as authenticated users, use your own with `setUserToken`. The `search-insights` library can create anonymous user tokens and store them in cookie. To use cookie-based anonymous tokens, initialize the library with [`useCookie`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights/init#param-use-cookie) set to `true`:
JavaScript

```
insightsClient("init", { appId, apiKey });
insightsClient("setUserToken", yourUserToken);

// or

insightsClient("init", { appId, apiKey, useCookie: true });

```

In older versions of the `search-insights` library (earlier than version 2.0), cookie-based anonymous tokens are on by default.
##  Manage the Insights library
Autocomplete loads the [`search-insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights) library for you from [jsDelivr](https://www.jsdelivr.com/). You don’t need to install it or set it up yourself. If you’re using a [Content Security Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CSP) to protect your site and you want to let Autocomplete load `search-insights` for you, make sure to add `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net` in your list of trusted sources for JavaScript.

```
script-src https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/

```

If you prefer hosting your own version of `search-insights`, you can add it to your project:
  1. [Install the Insights client](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights)
  2. [Initialize the Insights client](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights/init)

Autocomplete doesn’t load `search-insights` when it detects it on the page.
##  Default events
After enabling the [`insights` option](https://www.algolia.com/doc/ui-libraries/autocomplete/api-reference/autocomplete-js/autocomplete#param-insights), Autocomplete automatically sends the following events:  
| Event  | Description  |  
| --- | --- |  
| `Items Viewed`  |  [View events](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/sdk/v1/methods/viewed-object-ids) for results shown in the autocomplete menu.  |  
| `Items Selected`  |  [Click events](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/sdk/v1/methods/clicked-object-ids-after-search) when users selects an item in the menu.  |  
By default, Autocomplete doesn’t send any conversion events. You can [send events from templates](https://www.algolia.com/doc/ui-libraries/autocomplete/guides/sending-algolia-insights-events#send-events-from-templates) manually.
##  Customize events
You can customize the Insights plugin by using one of these hooks:

For example, you might want to use a different `eventName`. For more information, see the [examples](https://www.algolia.com/doc/ui-libraries/autocomplete/api-reference/autocomplete-plugin-algolia-insights/createAlgoliaInsightsPlugin) in the `createAlgoliaInsightsPlugin` documentation.
