To use Google Tag Manager (GTM) for sending [click and conversion events](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/sending-events) to the Algolia Insights API, you need to add data attributes to your website’s templates and configure the Algolia Insights template in the GTM dashboard.
##  Update your search parameters
To connect events to searches, including those from [category pages](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/solutions/ecommerce/browse/tutorials/category-pages), you must pass [`queryID`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/sending-events/guides/queryid) when sending search-related events to the Insights API, such as with the [`clickedObjectIDsAfterSearch`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/sdk/v1/methods/clicked-object-ids-after-search) method. To include the `queryID` in the search response, set [`clickAnalytics`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/clickAnalytics) to `true`. To identify users, [add the `userToken` parameter](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/sending-events/concepts/usertoken).
