Signature

```
singleIndex(
  indexName: string,
);

```

##  Import
Package manager
CDN

```
import { singleIndex } from "instantsearch.js/es/lib/stateMappings";

```


```
const { singleIndex } = instantsearch.stateMappings;
// or directly use instantsearch.stateMappings.singleIndex()

```

##  About this widget
The `singleIndex` state mapping can be applied to the `instantsearch` object’s [routing](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/js#param-routing) option. It enables backward compatibility with version 3.x. The mapping applies the following transformations:
  * Omits the `configure` widget
  * Uses the given index for the top level


JavaScript

```
singleIndex("instant_search").stateToRoute({
  instant_search: {
    query: "Apple",
    page: 5,
    configure: {
      hitsPerPage: 4,
    },
  },
});

// {
//   query: 'Apple',
//   page: 5,
// }

```

##  Examples
JavaScript

```
instantsearch({
  // ...
  routing: {
    stateMapping: singleIndex("instant_search"),
  },
});

```

##  Options
indexName
string
required
The name of the index to get the state from, usually the same value provided to [`instantsearch`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/js).
JavaScript

```
singleIndex("instant_search");

```

