##  Parameters
query
string
required
Search query.Use an empty query to fetch all objects.
browseParameters
object
Compatible [search parameters](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/search-api-parameters). For example:
  * Retrieve only certain attributes:
    * [`attributesToRetrieve`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/attributesToRetrieve)
  * Filtering:
    * [`facetFilters`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/facetFilters)
    * [`numericFilters`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/numericFilters)

When using `browse`, the engine overrides these API parameters:
  * [`typoTolerance`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/typoTolerance) can only be `true` or `false`. If you set [`typoTolerance`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/typoTolerance) to `min` or `strict`, the engine sets it to `true` (records matching up to 2 typos are retrieved)
  * [`distinct`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/distinct): `false`
  * [`enableRules`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/enableRules): `false`
  * [`ignorePlurals`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/ignorePlurals): `false`
  * [`advancedSyntax`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/advancedSyntax): `false`
  *   * [`getRankingInfo`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/getRankingInfo): `false`
  * [`attributesToHighlight`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/attributesToHighlight): `[]`
  * [`attributesToSnippet`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/attributesToSnippet): `[]`
  * [`optionalFilters`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/optionalFilters): `[]`

When using `browse`, the pagination parameters [`hitsPerPage`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/hitsPerPage) and [`page`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/page) are ignored.Personalization isn’t applied to browse requests. The [`enablePersonalization`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/api-parameters/enablePersonalization) parameter is ignored.
requestOptions
object
A mapping of request options to send along with the query.
##  Response
cursor
string
A cursor to retrieve the next chunk of objects. If absent, the end of the index has been reached.
hits
list
Retrieved records.
hitsPerPage
integer
The maximum number of hits returned per page. Present only when the query is empty and the browse is not filtered.
nbHits
integer
Number of objects in the index. Present only when the query is empty and the browse is not filtered.
nbPages
integer
The number of returned pages. Calculation is based on total number of hits (`nbHits`) divided by the number of hits per page (`hitsPerPage`), rounded to the nearest highest integer.Present only when the query is empty and the browse is not filtered.
page
integer
Index of the current page (zero-based). Present only when the query is empty and the browse is not filtered.
params
string
URL-encoded search parameters used to filter the results.
processingTimeMS
integer
Time that the server took to process the request, in milliseconds. This does not include network time.
query
string
Query text used to filter the results.
