##  About this widget
The `<InfiniteHits>` widget displays a list of results with a “Show more” button at the bottom of the list. As an alternative to this approach, [the infinite scroll guide](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/ui-and-ux-patterns/infinite-scroll/react) describes how to create an automatically scrolling infinite hits experience. See also: [Searches without results](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/going-further/conditional-display/react#handling-no-results)
You can also create your own UI with [`useInfiniteHits`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/infinite-hits/react#hook).
##  Examples
