##  Parameters
queries
object[]
required
A list of [queries](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/sdk/v1/methods/multiple-queries#param-query-object) to execute.
Show child attributes
indexName
string
required
Name of the index to target.
query
string
required
The query to search in the index.
params
object
A key/value mapping of any [search parameters](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/search-api-parameters)
type
string
default:"default"
The type of query to perform. Can be either `default` for a regular search, or `facet` for a [facet value search](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/sdk/v1/methods/search-for-facet-values).
requestOptions
object
A mapping of request options to send along with the query.
strategy
string
The _strategy_ of the query.Can be one of the following values:
  * `none`: Execute the sequence of queries until the end. This is recommended when each query is of equal importance, meaning all records of all queries need to be returned.
  * `stopIfEnoughMatches`: Execute queries one by one, but stop as soon as the cumulated number of hits is at least `hitsPerPage`. This is recommended when each query is an alternative, and where, if the first returns enough records, there is no need to perform the remaining queries.


