##  Accessing secured data
You can’t rely on filters to select what data to return to a specific user because users can change these parameters. If all you have to pick specific data is query time filters, anyone can alter these to access the data of another user. To properly restrict access of a user to only their data (and the public data), you need to use [secured API keys](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/security/api-keys). Without MCM, you need to set the filters to authorize manually.
