##  Hook
React InstantSearch let you create your own UI for the `<RelatedProducts>` widget with `useRelatedProducts`. Hooks provide APIs to access the widget state and interact with InstantSearch. The `useRelatedProducts` Hook accepts [parameters](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/related-products/react#parameters) and returns [APIs](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/related-products/react#hook). It must be used inside the [`<InstantSearch>`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/react) component.
###  Usage
First, create your React component:
JavaScript

```
import { useRelatedProducts } from "react-instantsearch";

function CustomRelatedProducts(props) {
  const { items } = useRelatedProducts(props);

  return <>{/*Your JSX*/}</>;


```

Then, render the widget:
JavaScript

```
<CustomRelatedProducts {...props} />

```

###  Parameters
Hooks accept parameters. You can either pass them manually or forward props from a custom component.
When passing functions to Hooks, ensure stable references to prevent unnecessary re-renders. Use [`useCallback()`](https://reactjs.org/docs/hooks-reference.html#usecallback) for memoization. Arrays and objects are automatically memoized.
