##  Build the autocomplete text box
When using [`autocomplete-core`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/ui-libraries/autocomplete/api-reference/autocomplete-core), you’re in control of rendering the entire experience using the Autocomplete state.
Create a custom hook
Create a custom hook that instantiates Autocomplete with the passed options and returns the instance and state.
JSX

```
import React from "react";
import { createAutocomplete } from "@algolia/autocomplete-core";

function useAutocomplete(props) {
  const [state, setState] = React.useState(() => ({
    collections: [],
    completion: null,
    context: {},
    isOpen: false,
    query: "",
    activeItemId: null,
    status: "idle",
  }));

  const autocomplete = React.useMemo(
    () =>
      createAutocomplete({
        ...props,
        onStateChange(params) {
          props.onStateChange?.(params);
          setState(params.state);
        },
      }),
    [],
  );

  return { autocomplete, state };


```

Build the Autocomplete component
Create an `Autocomplete` component which consumes the hook and renders the experience.
JSX

```
function Autocomplete(props) {
  const { autocomplete, state } = useAutocomplete({
    ...props,
    id: "twitter-autocomplete",
    defaultActiveItemId: 0,
  });

  return null;


```

Use the Autocomplete component in your app
In your `App.jsx` file, render the `Autocomplete` component and pass Autocomplete options as props.
