##  Import
Package manager
CDN

```
import { simple } from "instantsearch.js/es/lib/stateMappings";

```


```
const { simple } = instantsearch.stateMappings;
// or directly use instantsearch.stateMappings.simple()

```

##  About this widget
This `simple` state mapping is the default for the `instantsearch` object’s [routing](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/js#param-routing) option. The router provides an API that lets you customize some of its behaviors. To get a sense of what you can do with the API, see [Routing URLs](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/going-further/routing-urls/js). The only transformation applied by the function is the omission of `configure`.
JavaScript

```
simple().stateToRoute({
  instant_search: {
    query: "Apple",
    page: 5,
    configure: {
      hitsPerPage: 4,
    },
  },
});

// gives as output:
// {
//   instant_search: {
//     query: 'Apple',
//     page: 5,
//   },
// }

```

##  Examples
JavaScript

```
instantsearch({
  // ...
  routing: {
    stateMapping: simple(),
  },
});

```

