##  Import
Package manager
CDN

```
import instantsearch from 'instantsearch.js';

```


```
window.instantsearch;

```

##  About this widget
The `instantsearch` object is the root wrapper component for all widgets. Two parameters are required:
  * [`indexName`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/js#param-index-name). The main in which to search.
  * [`searchClient`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/js#param-search-client). The search client for InstantSearch.js. The [search client](https://github.com/algolia/algoliasearch-client-javascript) needs an `appId` and an `apiKey`, which you can find in the [Algolia dashboard](https://dashboard.algolia.com/account/api-keys).

See also: [Get started with InstantSearch.js](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/getting-started/js)
###  Middleware
InstantSearch.js provides middleware to help you connect to other systems:
  * **Insights**. Use the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/insights/js) middleware to [send click and conversion events](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/events/js)
  * **Generic**. With the [`middleware`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/middleware/js) API, you can inject logic into InstantSearch.js. For example, to [send events to Google Analytics](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/going-further/integrate-google-analytics/js).


##  Examples
JavaScript

```
const search = instantsearch({
  indexName: "INDEX_NAME",
  searchClient: algoliasearch("YourApplicationID", "YourSearchOnlyAPIKey"),
});

// Add widgets
// ...

search.start();

```

##  Options
indexName
string
required
The main index to search into.
JavaScript

```
const search = instantsearch({
  // ...
