  * **Type** : `function`

By default, the crawler adds URLs to the queue based on [`pathsToMatch`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/tools/crawler/apis/configuration/actions#param-paths-to-match), [`fileTypesToMatch`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/tools/crawler/apis/configuration/actions#param-file-types-to-match), and [`exclusionPatterns`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/tools/crawler/apis/configuration/exclusion-patterns). To customize this behavior, define a `linkExtractor` function. This function runs on every crawled page and returns a list of URLs as strings.
##  Examples
JavaScript

```

    linkExtractor: ({ $, url, defaultExtractor }) => {
      if (/example.com\/doc\//.test(url.href)) {
        // For all pages under /doc, only queue the first found link
        return defaultExtractor().slice(0,1);

      // Otherwise, use the default logic (queue all found links)
      return defaultExtractor();
    },


```

JavaScript

```

  linkExtractor: ({ $, url, defaultExtractor }) => {
    // This turns off link discovery, except for URLs listed in sitemap.xml
    return /sitemap.xml/.test(url.href) ? defaultExtractor() : [];
  },


```

JavaScript

```

  linkExtractor: ({ $ }) => {
    // Access the DOM and extract what you specify
    return [$('.my-link').attr('href')]
  },


```

