##  Import
Package manager
CDN

```
import { lookingSimilar } from 'instantsearch.js/es/widgets';

```


```
const { lookingSimilar } = instantsearch.widgets;
// or directly use instantsearch.widgets.lookingSimilar()

```

##  About this widget
Use the `lookingSimilar` widget to display a list of similar-looking products based on the image URLs you referenced when [setting up this Recommend model](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/algolia-recommend/how-to/lookingSimilar). See also: [Set up Algolia Recommend](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/algolia-recommend/how-to/set-up)
##  Examples
JavaScript

```
lookingSimilar({
  container: "#lookingSimilar",
  objectIDs: ["5723537"],
  templates: {
    item(recommendation, { html }) {
      return html`
        <h2>${recommendation.name}</h2>
        <p>${recommendation.description}</p>

    },
  },
});

```

###  With a carousel layout
Display the `lookingSimilar` widget as a [scrollable carousel](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/looking-similar/js#param-layout).
JavaScript

```
import { carousel } from "instantsearch.js/es/templates";
// or
const { carousel } = instantsearch.templates;

lookingSimilar({
  container: "#lookingSimilar",
  objectIDs: ["5723537"],
  templates: {
    item(recommendation, { html }) {
      return html`
        <h2>${recommendation.name}</h2>
        <p>${recommendation.description}</p>

    },
    layout: carousel(),
  },
});

```

