##  Customize the UI with `connectLookingSimilar`
If you want to create your own UI of the `lookingSimilar` widget, you can use connectors. To use `connectLookingSimilar`, you can import it with the declaration relevant to how you installed InstantSearch.js.
Package manager
CDN

```
import { connectLookingSimilar } from 'instantsearch.js/es/connectors';

```


```
const { connectLookingSimilar } = instantsearch.connectors;
// or directly use instantsearch.connectors.connectLookingSimilar()

```

Then it’s a 3-step process:
JavaScript

```
// 1. Create a render function
const renderLookingSimilar = (renderOptions, isFirstRender) => {
  // Rendering logic
};

// 2. Create the custom widget
const customLookingSimilar = connectLookingSimilar(renderLookingSimilar);

// 3. Instantiate
search.addWidgets([
  customLookingSimilar({
    // instance params
  }),
]);

```

###  Create a render function
This rendering function is called before the first search (`init` lifecycle step) and each time results come back from Algolia (`render` lifecycle step).
JavaScript

```
const renderLookingSimilar = (renderOptions, isFirstRender) => {
  const { items, widgetParams } = renderOptions;

  if (isFirstRender) {
    // Do some initial rendering and bind events


  // Render the widget
};

```

