If you’re using the deprecated [`recommend-js`](https://algolia.com/old-docs/deprecated/recommend/api-reference/recommend-js) UI library, see [`trendingItems`](https://algolia.com/old-docs/deprecated/recommend/api-reference/recommend-js/trendingItems).
Signature

```
trendingItems({
  container: string | HTMLElement,
  // Optional parameters
  facetName?: string,
  facetValue?: string,
  limit?: number,
  threshold?: number,
  queryParameters?: object,
  fallbackParameters?: object,
  escapeHTML?: boolean,
  templates?: object,
  cssClasses?: object,
  transformItems?: function,
});

```

##  Import
Package manager
CDN

```
import { trendingItems } from 'instantsearch.js/es/widgets';

```


```
const { trendingItems } = instantsearch.widgets;
// or directly use instantsearch.widgets.trendingItems()

```

##  About this widget
Use the `trendingItems` widget to display a list of trending items. See also: [Set up Algolia Recommend](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/algolia-recommend/how-to/set-up)
##  Examples
JavaScript

```
trendingItems({
  container: "#trendingItems",
  facetName: "category",
  facetValue: "Book",
  templates: {
    item(recommendation, { html }) {
      return html`
        <h2>${recommendation.name}</h2>
        <p>${recommendation.description}</p>

    },
  },
});

```

###  With a carousel layout
Display the `trendingItems` widget as a [scrollable carousel](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/trending-items/js#param-layout).
JavaScript

```
import { carousel } from "instantsearch.js/es/templates";
// or
const { carousel } = instantsearch.templates;

trendingItems({
  container: "#trendingItems",
  facetName: "category",
  facetValue: "Book",
  templates: {
    item(recommendation, { html }) {
      return html`
        <h2>${recommendation.name}</h2>
        <p>${recommendation.description}</p>

    },
    layout: carousel(),
  },
});

```

