##  Localized tags
You can prefix your tags with a locale, separated by a colon. For example, if the tags of an article are:
JavaScript

```
[ 'Wow', 'en:Awesome', 'en-gb:Good', 'fr:Incroyable' ]

```

The indices for each locale only contain the tags matching their locale:  
| Locales  | Tags  |  
| --- | --- |  
| All `fr` locales  | `{ "label_names": ["Incroyable"] }`  |  
| `en-gb`  | `{ label_names: ["Good"] }`  |  
| Other `en` locales, for example, `en-us`  | `{ "label_names": ["Awesome"] }`  |  
| All other locales  | `{ label_names: ["Wow"] }`  |  
