##  Keep the widget mounted but hidden
The most straightforward way to retain a widget’s state and refinements is to **avoid unmounting it**. You can, for example, hide the content of the dialog with CSS:

```
<template>
ais-instant-search
    :future="{ preserveSharedStateOnUnmount: true }"
    :search-client="searchClient"
    index-name="instant_search"

Search />
button type="button" @click="showMenu != showMenu">Filters</button>
ais-refinement-list v-show="showMenu" attribute="brand" />
  </ais-instant-search>
</template>

