###  Types
Types are now available in React InstantSearch v7. You can uninstall all InstantSearch types coming from [DefinitelyTyped](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped).
Command line

```
npm uninstall @types/react-instantsearch-dom @types/react-instantsearch-core @types/react-instantsearch

```

##  Migrate from React InstantSearch Hooks to React InstantSearch v7
From v7, React InstantSearch Hooks is called React InstantSearch. The migration is straightforward as the APIs are the same. Only package names have changed, and several APIs have been deprecated.
###  Package names  
| Before  | After  |  
| --- | --- |  
| `react-instantsearch-hooks`  | `react-instantsearch-core`  |  
| `react-instantsearch-hooks-web`  | `react-instantsearch`  |  
| `react-instantsearch-hooks-server`  | `react-instantsearch`  |  
| `react-instantsearch-hooks-router-nextjs`  | `react-instantsearch-router-nextjs`  |  
Update your `package.json` file:
package.json

```

  "dependencies": {
-   "react-instantsearch-hooks": "^6.42.0",
+   "react-instantsearch-core": "^7.0.0",
-   "react-instantsearch-hooks-web": "^6.42.0",
+   "react-instantsearch": "^7.0.0",
-   "react-instantsearch-hooks-server": "^6.42.0",
-   "react-instantsearch-hooks-router-nextjs": "^6.42.0",
+   "react-instantsearch-router-nextjs": "^7.0.0",



```

After updating your `package.json` file, run `npm install` to install the updated dependencies. You can then change your imports:
JavaScript

```
-import { useInstantSearch } from 'react-instantsearch-hooks';
+import { useInstantSearch } from 'react-instantsearch-core';
-import { SearchBox } from 'react-instantsearch-hooks-web';
-import { getServerState } from 'react-instantsearch-hooks-server';
+import { SearchBox, getServerState } from 'react-instantsearch';
-import { createInstantSearchRouterNext } from 'react-instantsearch-hooks-router-nextjs';
+import { createInstantSearchRouterNext } from 'react-instantsearch-router-nextjs';

```

The `react-instantsearch-hooks-server` functions are now included in `react-instantsearch`.
###  Codemods
To automatically update your code to use the new package names and APIs from React InstantSearch v7, Algolia provides a [codemod](https://www.codeshiftcommunity.com/docs/). First, uninstall the `react-instantsearch-hooks-*` packages and install their `react-instantsearch-*` counterparts.
Command line

```
npm uninstall react-instantsearch-hooks-web react-instantsearch-hooks react-instantsearch-hooks-server
npm install react-instantsearch react-instantsearch-core

```

Assuming your source code is in the `src/` folder, run the following command:
Command line

```
npx @codeshift/cli -e js,jsx,ts,tsx --packages 'instantsearch-codemods#rish-to-ris' src/

```

Afterwards you should run your code formatter as codemods might output code that doesn’t follow your code style:
yarn
npm

```
yarn prettier --write 'src/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}'
# or
yarn eslint --fix src/

```


```
npm exec prettier --write 'src/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}'
# or
npm exec eslint --fix src/

```

###  `use` to `addMiddlewares`
[`useInstantSearch`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/use-instantsearch/react)’s `use` function has been renamed to `addMiddlewares`.
JavaScript

```
import { useInstantSearch } from 'react-instantsearch-core';

function Middleware() {
- const { use } = useInstantSearch();
+ const { addMiddlewares } = useInstantSearch();

  useEffect(() => {
    const middleware = /* ... */;

-   return use(middleware);
+   return addMiddlewares(middleware);
- }, [use]);
+ }, [addMiddlewares]);

  return null;


```

###  `getServerState`
The [`getServerState`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/server-state/react) function now requires `renderToString` from `react-dom/server` to be passed as a second argument.
JavaScript

```
+import { renderToString } from 'react-dom/server';
import { getServerState } from 'react-instantsearch';

function App() {
  return (
    /* ... */
  );


async function getServerSideProps() {
- const serverState = await getServerState(<App />);
+ const serverState = await getServerState(<App />, { renderToString });

  return {
    props: {
      serverState,
    },
  };


```

###  `Stats`
The `translations` prop of the [`Stats`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/stats/react) widget has changed and now accepts a `rootElementText` function instead of a `stats` function.
React

```
function Search() {
  return (
    <Stats
      translations={{
-       stats({ nbHits, processingTimeMS }) {
+       rootElementText({ nbHits, processingTimeMS }) {
          return `${nbHits.toLocaleString()} results found in ${processingTimeMS.toLocaleString()}ms`;
        },
      }}
    />
  );


```

##  Upgrade event tracking
**Starting from v6.43.0, React InstantSearch Hooks simplifies the event tracking process with the[`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/react#param-insights) option.** You no longer need to install the [`search-insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights) library or set up the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/insights/react) middleware yourself. Here are some benefits when using the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/react#param-insights) option:
  * It better handles the . Once you set it, all search and event tracking calls include the token.
  * It automatically sends default events from built-in widgets such as [`RefinementList`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/refinement-list/react), [`Menu`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/menu/react), etc. You can also change the event payloads, or remove them altogether.
  * It lets you send custom events from your custom widgets.
  * It simplifies forwarding events to third-party trackers.

If you’ve been tracking events directly with [`search-insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights) or with the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/insights/react) middleware, you should:
  1. Upgrade `react-instantsearch-hooks` to v6.43.0 or greater
  2. [Migrate](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/upgrade-guides/react#use-the-insights-option) from using the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/insights/react) middleware to the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/react#param-insights) option
  3. Either [update](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/upgrade-guides/react#update-search-insights) or [remove](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/upgrade-guides/react#remove-search-insights) the [`search-insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights) library


###  Use the `insights` option
**Starting from v6.43.0, InstantSearch lets you enable event tracking with the[`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/react#param-insights) option.** You no longer need to set up the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/insights/react) middleware yourself.
React

```
function App() {
  return (
InstantSearch
      // ...
      insights={true}

/* Widgets */}
    </InstantSearch>
  );


```

If you had already set up the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/insights/react) middleware in your code, you can now remove it and move its configuration to the [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/react#param-insights) option.
React

```
-import { createInsightsMiddleware } from 'instantsearch.js/es/middlewares';
-import { useInstantSearch } from 'react-instantsearch-hooks-web';
-import { useLayoutEffect } from 'react';
import { liteClient as algoliasearch } from 'algoliasearch/lite';

- function InsightsMiddleware() {
-   const { addMiddlewares } = useInstantSearch();

-   useLayoutEffect(() => {
-     const middleware = createInsightsMiddleware({
-       insightsClient: window.aa,
-       insightsInitParams: {
-         useCookie: false,
-       }
-     });

-     return addMiddlewares(middleware);
-   }, [addMiddlewares]);

-   return null;
-}

function App() {
  return (
    <InstantSearch
      // ...
+      insights={{
+        insightsInitParams: {
+          useCookie: false,
+        }
+      }}

      <InsightsMiddleware />
      {/* Widgets */}
    </InstantSearch>
  );


```

###  Update `search-insights`
**Starting from v4.55.0, InstantSearch can load[`search-insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights) for you so the [`insightsClient`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/insights/react#param-insights-client) option is no longer required.** If you prefer loading it yourself, make sure to update [`search-insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/libraries/search-insights) to at least v2.4.0 and forward the reference to [`insights`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/instantsearch/react#param-insights). If you’re using the UMD bundle with a `script` tag, make sure to update the full code snippet (not just the version):
